CRS benchmark reference data
----------------------------
The pair-4979-4978, pair-mars-iau, form-27700-projjson, seed-tpers, edge-tpers-back,
seed-igh, seed-ob_tran-moll, method-qsc, method-healpix and method-rhealpix numeric fixtures are from Michael Sumner's rust-proj-capability
(https://github.com/mdsumner/rust-proj-capability), revision
ddd9fac70ec370acd9651ebb8b46035207347ad5, generated with PROJ 9.9.0.
The CRS-study oracle version is retained separately from projection-suite data.

IAU_2015 registry and celestial-body compatibility
-------------------------------------------------
The bundled IAU_2015 definitions are derived from PROJ 9.8.1's data/sql/iau.sql,
Git blob 900564ccf2e1f77fb708ddc2c8544843b29bc24a, generated by
scripts/build_db_from_iau.py (Copyright (c) 2021, Hobu Inc; author Even Rouault),
under PROJ's MIT terms reproduced above. The source planetary reference is the
IAU Working Group report at https://doi.org/10.1007/s10569-017-9805-5 .
The celestial-body compatibility rule follows PROJ 9.8.1's
src/iso19111/operation/coordinateoperationfactory.cpp and
include/proj/internal/datum_internal.hpp (0.7% semi-major-axis allowance), and
its Earth-radius heuristic follows src/iso19111/datum.cpp, under the same terms.
The conformal-sphere radius calculation (+R_C) follows PROJ 9.8.1's
src/ell_set.cpp, under the same MIT terms.
The inverse authalic-latitude refinement for large flattening follows
src/latitudes.cpp from PROJ 9.8.1, under the same terms.
The forward authalic-latitude series (C[xi,phi]) follows src/latitudes.cpp from PROJ 9.8.1,
under the same terms.
The sixth-order meridian-distance series follows PROJ 9.8.1's src/mlfn.cpp
and src/latitudes.cpp (Karney's auxiliary-latitude series), under the same terms.
